# Trivy image-scan suppressions for the release publication gate.
#
# Policy: only findings that exist in the LATEST published base images and are
# owned by the base-image upstream (Debian / Docker Official Images) may be
# listed here. Each entry needs a rationale and a review date; when the base
# images are refreshed (see docs/development.md "Base image updates"), re-scan
# the bases and delete entries that no longer appear.
#
# Base images at time of entry:
#   python:3.12-slim@sha256:09f7da3bc104798d0afb40bc08d23ab2da20a76130cec1f2ef170848f5d85217
#   docker:29.7.2-cli@sha256:3f4743208d2338c934d7b8bcfbe1bb54c0b2355c510ad5e0f31c0c4a54bd704e
#   (the sandbox-controller build additionally runs `apk upgrade --no-cache`
#   at build time, so Alpine OS-package findings below the pinned digest are
#   fixed, not suppressed)
# Reviewed: 2026-09-03

# Debian has not yet rebuilt python:3.12-slim with the openssl fix; the
# advisory is HIGH DoS-class in the legacy provider subpackage. Present in
# every current python:3.12-slim digest. Re-check on next base refresh.
CVE-2026-14456

